    {
      "id": 116651,
      "name": "Ryan Johnson",
      "username": "Ryan_Johnson",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/6f9a4e/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-09-25T20:03:32.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Sentinels Fans of the Twin Cities! &nbsp;I have dire news and urgent announcemnets. &nbsp;</p><p>First, the events are being pushed back a bit due to a scheduling snafu. &nbsp;</p><p>The Southdale event will now be on October 2nd, and the Burnsville event will now be on October 9th. &nbsp;</p><p>We apologize whole-heartedly for any inconveinance this may cause you. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, to answer a couple concerns:&nbsp;</p><p>Each table fights the same villain each round, so Baron Blade would be removed from the pool after being defeated. &nbsp;We are only using base set villains since not every fan has each expansion. &nbsp;</p><p>The promo cards are the Dark Watch series, which is a set of 6 (4 heores, 2 villains). &nbsp;We are leaving it to the players to determine how to divide them amongst themselves as we do not have enough to give every player who attends a set. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We hope to see you Thursday!</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:49:07.634Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
